# OAuth client id for pushing to Google Calendar.
#
# Create it at console.cloud.google.com: enable the Google Calendar API, add
# yourself as a test user on the OAuth consent screen, then create an OAuth
# client id of type "Web application" with http://localhost:5173 as an
# authorized JavaScript origin. See the README for the full walkthrough.
#
# There is no client secret - the browser-side flow does not use one, which is
# why this file is safe to describe here and unsafe only if you commit .env.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
